.TH SIN 3M
.SH NAME
sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan, atan2 \- trigonometric functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <math.h>"
.sp
.B "double sin(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double cos(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double asin(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double acos(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double atan(x)"
.B "double x;"
.sp
.B "double atan2(x, y)"
.B "double x, y;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sin ,
.BR cos ,
and
.B tan
return trigonometric functions of radian arguments.
The magnitude of the argument should be checked by the caller to make
sure the result is meaningful.
.PP
.B asin
returns the arc sin of
.I x
in the range \-pi/2 to pi/2.
.PP
.B acos
returns the arc cosine of
.I x
in the range 0 to pi.
.PP
.B atan
returns the arc tangent of
.I x
in the range \-pi/2 to pi/2.
.PP
.B atan2
returns the arc tangent of
.I x/y
in the range \-pi to pi.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Arguments of magnitude greater than 1 cause
.B asin
and
.B acos
to return
value 0;
.B errno
is set to EDOM.
The value of
.B tan
at its singular points is
a huge number, and
.B errno
is set to ERANGE.
.SH BUGS
The value of
.B tan
for arguments greater than about 2**31 is garbage.
.sp
